<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <a href="/manage/feedback">Lanyard Feedback</a> collects what staff at every company have said about Lanyard:
        thumbs up or down from the feedback button in the top bar, and star ratings from the occasional
        "How would you rate Lanyard?" prompt. Only platform admins can open it, and the
        <strong>Lanyard Feedback</strong> menu item shows how many are still waiting to be reviewed.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Finding feedback">
        <ol>
            <li>Pick <strong>All</strong>, <strong>Good</strong>, <strong>Not great</strong> or <strong>Star ratings</strong> to choose which kind to show.</li>
            <li>Leave <strong>Unreviewed only</strong> on to see just what you haven't dealt with yet. Turn it off to see everything.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            The line above the cards totals what's shown: how many, how many were good or not great, and the
            average star rating. It follows the filters. The most recent 300 are shown, newest first.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="What each card shows">
        <ul>
            <li>The verdict (<strong>Good</strong> or <strong>Not great</strong>) or the number of stars, and a
                <FluentBadge Appearance="BadgeAppearance.Tint" Color="BadgeColor.Brand">New</FluentBadge> badge until it's reviewed.</li>
            <li>The comment, or "No comment" if they didn't leave one.</li>
            <li>Who sent it and their email, their company and location, when they sent it (UK time) and a link to the page they were on.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Dealing with feedback">
        <ol>
            <li>Press <strong>Reply</strong> to start an email to the person in your own mail app. It's only there when they have an email address.</li>
            <li>Press <strong>Mark reviewed</strong> once you've dealt with it. It drops out of the <strong>Unreviewed only</strong> view and the menu count.</li>
            <li>Changed your mind? Turn <strong>Unreviewed only</strong> off and press <strong>Mark unreviewed</strong>.</li>
        </ol>
        <HelpNote>
            Every platform admin with an email address is also emailed each piece of feedback as it arrives,
            with a link back to this page. If the email fails, the feedback is still saved here.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
